[center][size=6][b]HEEL OF ACHILLES[/b][/size]
[i]One cut. They never stand up again.[/i][/center]

Get behind them and slash the back of the heel. Half of them die on the spot. The rest go down for good and keep fighting from the ground. No more trading blows with a tank: find the one spot that matters and win with skill, not force.

[center][img]{{GIF_CUT}}[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]How it plays[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The cut.[/b] Slash or stab the back of the heel, from behind or the side. Blunt hits and hits from the front do nothing. Swords, thrown daggers and spells all work.
[*][b]Instant death.[/b] By default half of all cuts kill on the spot, with the game's own death animation. It counts as your kill.
[*][b]Down for good.[/b] The rest drop and never get up. Each one rolls its own fate: most sit down and drag themselves after you, some fall to their knees and fight on, a few just lie there.
[*][b]Still dangerous.[/b] They scream, crawl toward you and swing from the ground. Not all of them, though. Good luck guessing which. They turn slowly, so circle around them.
[*][b]Bleeding out.[/b] Blood drips from the cut. They get slower and quieter, start gasping and die after about 45 seconds. Or you end it sooner.
[/list]

[center][img]{{GIF_INSTANT}}[/img]
